From: Steve Slivinski <stesli@github.local>
Subject: [PATCH] shared_image: keep whole P010 format for Pi5 SAND128 per-plane import

Fixes a 10-bit HEVC (Main10) black-video regression introduced when the
local patch set was ported from Chromium 147 to 151.

On the Pi 5 V4L2 HEVC path the decoder emits BROADCOM SAND128 column-tiled
buffers; 10-bit content is packed as P030 (three 10-bit samples per 32-bit
word), which Mesa v3d only samples correctly when the EGL/gbm dma-buf import
is tagged with a P010 fourcc that patches 0011/0012 then remap to P030.
External sampling is deliberately disabled (patch 0015), so these frames
take the per-plane multiplanar path (target=GL_TEXTURE_2D, one texture per
plane).

On 147, OzoneImageGLTexturesHolder::GetBinding passed the whole kP010
SharedImageFormat into ImportNativePixmap even on the per-plane path, so the
P010->P030 remap fired and 10-bit rendered. Upstream 151 changed the
per-plane branch to substitute the single-channel plane format
(GetFormatForPlane -> R16 / GR1616). With the format no longer equal to
kP010, the remap guard (fcc == DRM_FORMAT_P010) never matches, the buffer is
imported as an untiled R16/GR1616 dma-buf, and Mesa samples garbage ->
uniform black 10-bit video (audio unaffected). 8-bit NV12 (R8 / GR88) is
unaffected because its per-plane single-channel import is valid for SAND128
once the modifier is present (patch 0017).

Runtime diagnostics (patch 0016) confirmed 147 vs 151 produce a
byte-identical per-plane import (same fds, offsets, pitch=1632,
modifier=0x700000000000004, plane sizes 1920x1080 / 960x540) and differ only
in that the P010->P030 remap fires on 147 but not on 151.

Fix: in the per-plane branch, keep the whole kP010 format (so the existing
remap fires) specifically for BROADCOM-modifier kP010 buffers, while still
setting buffer_plane_index / per-plane plane_size exactly as 147 did. All
other formats keep the upstream per-plane single-channel format.

--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/ozone_image_gl_textures_holder.cc
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/ozone_image_gl_textures_holder.cc
@@ -83,7 +83,24 @@
     plane_size = size;
     buffer_plane_index = std::nullopt;
   } else {
-    plane_format = GetFormatForPlane(format, plane_index);
+    // AGORA_PATCH_0021: Pi5 V4L2 HEVC 10-bit (kP010) capture buffers use the
+    // BROADCOM SAND128 column-tiled modifier and are packed as P030 (three
+    // 10-bit samples per 32-bit word), NOT P010 (10-bit padded to 16). Mesa
+    // v3d only samples them correctly when the EGL/gbm import is tagged with
+    // the whole kP010 format, which patches 0011/0012 then remap to P030.
+    // Upstream 151 began substituting the per-plane R16/GR1616 single-channel
+    // format here (147 kept the whole format), which silenced that remap and
+    // produced black 10-bit video. Keep the whole kP010 format for this case
+    // so the remap fires, while still importing per-plane (buffer_plane_index
+    // set) exactly as the working 147 build did. 8-bit NV12 (R8/GR88) is
+    // unaffected and keeps the per-plane single-channel format path below.
+    const uint64_t agora_modifier = pixmap->GetFormatModifier();
+    const bool agora_is_broadcom_sand_p010 =
+        format == viz::MultiPlaneFormat::kP010 &&
+        (agora_modifier >> 56) == 7 /* BROADCOM */;
+    if (!agora_is_broadcom_sand_p010) {
+      plane_format = GetFormatForPlane(format, plane_index);
+    }
     plane_size = format.GetPlaneSize(plane_index, size);
     buffer_plane_index = plane_index;
   }
